Unit tests for the µController source.

Run on the host, no board or hardware attached:

    pio test -e native

`test_rpm_counter/` exercises `src/logic/RpmCounter` — the tachometer
edge-counting and RPM calculation pulled out of `arduino_target.ino`'s
TimerHandler0 into a plain C++ class with no Arduino.h dependency, so it
can run natively instead of needing a real sensor and platter to test
against. `arduino_target.ino` itself, and anything under `src/data`, depend
on Arduino.h/BLE and can't be built for the `native` environment — see
`platformio.ini`'s `build_src_filter` for the `[env:native]` env.

More on PlatformIO Unit Testing: https://docs.platformio.org/page/plus/unit-testing.html
